  "details": "When using avatars with basically anything that doesnt have completely basic humanoid proportions the game will place you in the floor (In VR), this is done to scale the player using determinations based on the wing span and proportions, because of this avatars with for example extra long arms (Eg the Minecraft Iron Golem which I first found out about this system from).\nI created a Vrchat avatar that also has slighty strange proportions as apart of it and I havent found any workaround to trick the wingspan system (but if anyone knows one that would really help) and I think there should be a manual way to set the players height/floor and in my mind should be equally as crucial as being able to set the view of an avatar.",
